[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, white matte ceramic bowls placed side-by-side on an aged, dark-stained oak wood kitchen table with subtle grain textures and faint use marks. The camera angle is 3/4 overhead at 40 degrees, ensuring the interior of both bowls is fully visible. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, while the second sits slightly further back with a soft, natural bokeh effect. The chocolate peanut butter banana nice cream has a dense, thick, swirled soft-serve texture, showing a deep, rich cocoa-brown color with subtle lighter streaks from the blended banana and yogurt. The surface of each scoop is topped with a scattering of dark chocolate chips, some slightly pressed into the cream. Lighting is soft, natural side-light coming from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the cool, creamy sheen of the frozen mixture. A wooden spoon rests casually on the table near the foreground bowl. A few stray chocolate chips and a small smear of the blended banana mixture are visible on the wood surface near the bowl rims. The scene is authentic and lived-in, capturing the end of the cooking process. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The bowls look like a homemade, nourishing dessert for two. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional food photograph for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
